## Add Neo4j card to Back End settings page

### Context

The Back End page (Settings → Triple Store → Back End) only showed Lakebase and Delta.
Neo4j was already a supported graph engine (from PR#47) but was hidden behind a
legacy dropdown. Added a third card for Neo4j at parity with the other two backends.

### Changes

1. **src/front/templates/settings.html** — Added Neo4j card to the backend card grid;
   changed grid columns from `col-md-6` (2-col) to `col-md-4` (3-col); updated helper
   text. Neo4j card pre-selected server-side when `graph_engine == "neo4j"`.

2. **src/front/static/config/js/settings.js**:
   - `isNeo4jCardSelected()` helper added.
   - `applyNeo4jCardFromEngine()` helper selects the Neo4j card when engine=neo4j.
   - `loadTripleStoreBackend()` now also fetches `/settings/graph-engine` in parallel
     and selects the Neo4j card when graph_engine=neo4j.
   - `saveGraphDbSettings()` translates the Neo4j card selection to
     `triple_store_backend=lakebase` + `graph_engine=neo4j` before posting.
   - Radio change listener triggers `applyNeo4jAuthMethodVisibility()` and
     `prefillNeo4jConnectionFromConfig()` when Neo4j card is selected.

### Modified files

- `src/front/templates/settings.html`
- `src/front/static/config/js/settings.js`

### Test results

`uv run pytest -q -m "not scenario"` (settings + contract) → 161 passed, 2 pre-existing failures.

