## Per-domain graph backend selection (moved out of global Settings)

### Context

The graph backend (Lakebase / Delta / Neo4j) was an instance-wide global setting chosen in
Settings → Triple Store → Back End. Moved the *selection* to a mandatory per-domain choice in
Domain → Information → Knowledge Graph, exposed as a single unified dropdown. The backend
selector was removed from admin Settings. Engine *connection* config (Neo4j Bolt creds, Lakebase
schema/sync, Delta SQL warehouse) stays workspace-global — only the selection moved.

### Changes

1. **src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py** — Added the unified per-domain vocabulary
   (`GRAPH_BACKENDS`, `DEFAULT_GRAPH_BACKEND`, `normalize_graph_backend`) and `_resolve_graph_backend`.
   Rewrote `_resolve_triple_store_backend` / `_resolve_graph_engine` to read
   `DomainSession.info['graph_backend']` and map it (`lakebase`→lakebase, `databricks`→delta,
   `neo4j`→lakebase+neo4j). `_resolve_graph_engine_config` now only reads global connection config;
   removed the `domain.settings['registry']` selection mirror.

2. **src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py** — Seeded `info['graph_backend'] = "lakebase"` in the
   empty-domain template.

3. **src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py** — `save_domain_info` persists a validated `graph_backend`;
   `get_domain_info` / `get_domain_template_data` expose it; added `_coerce_graph_backend` validator
   (defaults to `lakebase`).

4. **src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py** — `resolve_graph_engine` now returns the resolved
   per-domain engine (no longer collapses everything to `lakebase`).

5. **src/back/objects/session/GlobalConfigService.py** — Removed `get/set_graph_engine`,
   `get/set_triple_store_backend`, `ALLOWED_GRAPH_ENGINES`, `ALLOWED_TRIPLE_STORE_BACKENDS`, and the
   `graph_engine` / `triple_store_backend` keys from `_empty()`. Kept `graph_engine_config`.

6. **src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py** — Removed `get/set_graph_engine_result` and
   `set_triple_store_backend_result`; replaced `get_triple_store_backend_result` with
   `get_delta_warehouse_result` (drops backend/allowed fields, keeps Delta warehouse + registry info);
   dropped `graph_engine` from `build_registry_get_payload`; simplified
   `_mirror_graph_engine_to_domain_registry` to connection-only (config + delta_warehouse_id).

7. **src/api/routers/internal/settings.py** — Removed GET/POST `/graph-engine` and
   `/triple-store-backend` selection endpoints; added GET `/delta-warehouse`.

8. **src/shared/fastapi/main.py** — Updated the permission-middleware read-only exception list
   (`/settings/graph-engine` → `/settings/delta-warehouse`).

9. **src/front/routes/home.py** — Settings page no longer resolves a global `graph_engine`.

10. **src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html** — Added the mandatory
    `#domainGraphBackend` dropdown to the Knowledge Graph tab with a rebuild warning.

11. **src/front/static/domain/js/domain.js** — Added `graph_backend` to the `saveDomainInfo` payload.

12. **src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js** — Loads/refreshes the backend dropdown.

13. **src/front/templates/settings.html** — Removed the backend radio cards + legacy engine select;
    replaced with an info banner pointing to the per-domain choice.

14. **src/front/static/config/js/settings.js** — Removed selection helpers/wiring; renamed
    `loadTripleStoreBackend` → `loadDeltaWarehouseState` (GET `/settings/delta-warehouse`);
    `saveGraphDbSettings` now persists only connection config + Delta warehouse.

15. **tests** — Updated `test_triple_store_backend_config.py`, `test_graph_engine_config.py`,
    `test_delta_warehouse_config.py`, `test_permission_middleware.py` for the new per-domain design.

