## Separate per-backend graph_engine_config (lakebase / neo4j)

Context: Admin requirement that each graph backend's connection config is
stored totally separately (nothing in common). The previous flat shared
`graph_engine_config` blob let Neo4j and Lakebase collide on `database`
(Lakebase health probing Postgres DB `neo4j`). Nest `{lakebase:{}, neo4j:{}}`
with read-time migration of legacy flat blobs; Delta stays on top-level
`delta_warehouse_id`.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/engine_config.py
   New normalizer + `lakebase_section` / `neo4j_section` helpers.

2. src/back/objects/session/GlobalConfigService.py
   get/set always normalize to nested shape; validate Lakebase keys on the
   lakebase bucket only.

3. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py + consumers (SettingsService,
   health.py, DigitalTwin, _build_pipeline, dtwin)
   Pass only the relevant backend section into constructors / probes.

4. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
   Settings → Back end panels read/write `lakebase` / `neo4j` buckets;
   client-side flat→nested migrate on load/save.

5. docs/graphdb-integration.md + docs/lakebase-graphdb.md
   Document nested storage and independent admin setup.

6. tests/units/graphdb/test_graph_engine_config_keys.py +
   tests/units/settings/test_graph_engine_config.py +
   tests/units/settings/test_neo4j_settings_persistence.py
   Cover migrate, nested resolvers, GlobalConfigService/SettingsService.

